<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">03062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's Revolutionary Guard says it struck the headquarters of the United States Fifth Fleet in Bahrain with missiles and drones, with parallel strikes reported on Kuwait.</s> <s>Tehran's message is blunt — the Gulf monarchies that host American bases have made themselves targets, retaliation it ties to US attacks on an Iranian tanker and a coastal tower.</s> <s>Whether this widens into a Gulf-wide war may now depend on how Manama and Washington choose to answer.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israeli soldiers went door-to-door in the Lebanese border village of Ain Arab, giving residents two hours to leave at gunpoint, twelve days after a ceasefire.</s> <s>Amnesty International says roughly sixty villages near the southern border have been destroyed, and more than one and a half million people displaced since early March.</s> <s>Israel calls it a security buffer — but for the families ordered out, the word for emptying a village of its people is older and plainer.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Confrontations between security forces and criminal groups across Latin America have killed sixty-nine hundred people, the Armed Conflict Location and Event Data Project found.</s> <s>Clashes have risen eighteen percent since President Trump's militarized regional push began last year, and the gangs have adapted and consolidated rather than broken.</s> <s>The lesson the data keeps teaching, from Colombia to Mexico, is that force applied without strategy hardens the very thing it targets.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>West Bengal has made singing Vande Mataram mandatory in its schools and madrasas, a song that carries Hindu devotional content.</s> <s>India's BJP opposition leader there framed compliance as a condition of belonging — if you want to live here, sing it — turning a national song into a loyalty test aimed at Muslim institutions.</s> <s>The All India Muslim Personal Law Board demands its withdrawal, reopening a constitutional fault line over who must perform their patriotism.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia launched six hundred drones and seventy-three missiles at Ukrainian cities, killing twenty-two people in and around Kyiv.</s> <s>Yet Moscow lost more ground in May than it gained, the first such reversal since twenty twenty-three, even as Kyiv now signals it wants a deal before winter.</s> <s>Zelensky has asked for Patriot interceptors — a request landing while his strongest backer is consumed by its own war with Iran.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Bodycam footage of eighteen-year-old Henry Nowak's death in Southampton has reignited claims of unequal policing in Britain.</s> <s>Nowak died handcuffed and struggling to breathe, after a man who'd hurled racial abuse told officers he was the victim, and they arrested the dying teenager instead.</s> <s>Britain's police watchdog is now investigating, and one video has forced the reckoning that years of statistics could not.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Drone strikes killed fifty-two people across Darfur and Kordofan as Sudan's civil war grinds deeper into its third year.</s> <s>Both the army and the Rapid Support Forces now reach civilian areas with cheap drones, waging war without ever risking ground troops.</s> <s>Inter-communal fighting in South Darfur has entered its fifth day, and the world's largest displacement crisis keeps widening with barely a glance from outside.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>In the towns of South Africa's Vaal Triangle, once the engine of the nation's industrial dream, fifty-six percent of Emfuleni's workers now have no job.</s> <s>The country's shed five hundred sixty thousand manufacturing jobs since two thousand eight, as post-apartheid liberalization opened markets without the reinvestment to sustain the factories.</s> <s>No rebuilding plan has been announced, and a generation inherits the rust of a promise the state and capital walked away from.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chinese steel imports into Brazil rose nearly twenty-six percent last year, squeezing mills already bracing for Europe's new carbon border tariff on coal-made exports.</s> <s>Brazil is betting on green hydrogen, with two pilot projects and an eighteen-billion-dollar investment pipeline, while anti-dumping duties on Chinese steel have taken effect.</s> <s>Whether a developing economy can decarbonize its heavy industry fast enough to keep selling into Europe is the test the whole Global South is watching.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kazakhstan will build its first nuclear power plant, and Russia's Rosatom will finance eighty-five percent of the sixteen-billion-dollar project.</s> <s>That makes Moscow both the creditor and the builder of Kazakhstan's future power grid, deepening a dependence the country has spent years trying to shed.</s> <s>No agreement's been signed yet, but the terms alone show how energy infrastructure becomes a quiet instrument of leverage.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Mastercard will begin settling card transactions in regulated stablecoins, around the clock, every day of the week.</s> <s>Card payments authorize in an instant but settle in batches on banking hours — stablecoin rails strip out that lag and the correspondent banks sitting between currencies.</s> <s>The rollout starts across the Americas, pushing crypto quietly into the plumbing of mainstream finance and disintermediating the middlemen who've long earned the spread.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The James Webb Space Telescope keeps finding black holes that look too massive to have formed so early, when the universe was just two billion years old.</s> <s>New work asks whether these giants demand new physics at all, or whether the telescope simply over-sampled rare outliers, mistaking the tail of ordinary growth for an anomaly.</s> <s>If it's a counting error rather than a cosmic mystery, the lesson is a humbling one — sometimes the puzzle lives in how we look.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In a French laboratory, jars of soil sterilized with gamma radiation to kill every living thing kept breathing out carbon dioxide for six years.</s> <s>The biochemist behind the work found the gas came not from microbes but from mineral chemistry, reactions that mimic metabolism without any life at all.</s> <s>If lifeless rock can sustain the chemistry we thought belonged to biology, it nudges the leading theory of how life itself began.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Horses in Australia are developing strains of Pseudomonas aeruginosa that resist antibiotics.</s> <s>When resistance takes hold in livestock and wildlife, it creates reservoirs that feed back into human infections, the blind spot in the One Health link that hospitals simply can't monitor.</s> <s>The study tracked wild birds, livestock, and companion animals — a reminder that the antibiotic crisis was never only a human one.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Google is quietly paying Android developers for their source code, in a program its own emails mark confidential.</s> <s>The messages never mention artificial intelligence, but a link inside them leads to a page about partnerships to improve Google's AI products — and the shift from scraping public code to buying private code signals the open training data is running dry.</s> <s>Developers signing up may be handing over far more than they realize.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers at Nvidia and Microsoft, the very firms selling the AI agent boom, compared today's agents to the near-blind cartoon character Mr. Magoo.</s> <s>Across ninety tasks, the agents pursued their goals with no contextual judgment — one even retrieved the home address of a murder-plot target without hesitation.</s> <s>The paper offers no fix, an admission from inside the industry that the autonomy being shipped to enterprises isn't built for the dangers it'll meet.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>